# Code Style

## Formatting

- Indentation: 2 spaces (no tabs)
- Quotes: single quotes for all strings (`'text'`, not `"text"`)
- Semicolons: always
- Line length: 100 characters max
- Trailing commas: ES5 style (yes in objects/arrays, no after last function param)
- Arrow parens: omit when possible (`x => x`, not `(x) => x`)
- Line endings: LF

```typescript
// CORRECT
const name = 'Stride';
const items = ['one', 'two', 'three'];
const fn = x => x * 2;

// WRONG
const name = "Stride"
const fn = (x) => x * 2
```

## Naming Conventions

| Thing | Convention | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Files (types, entities, enums) | PascalCase | `Spec.ts`, `SourceType.ts` |
| Files (repos, services, hooks) | kebab-case | `spec.repo.ts`, `spec.service.ts`, `useAuth.ts` |
| Files (React components) | PascalCase | `SpecCard.tsx`, `BacklogView.tsx` |
| Files (CSS Modules) | PascalCase matching component | `SpecCard.module.css` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `SpecService`, `SpecRepository` |
| Instances/singletons | camelCase | `specService`, `specRepo` |
| Functions | camelCase | `toDomain`, `generateId` |
| React components | PascalCase function | `function BacklogView()` |
| Hooks | camelCase with `use` prefix | `useAuth`, `useQueueStatus` |
| Types (domain entities) | PascalCase | `type Spec = { ... }` |
| Types (inputs/DTOs) | PascalCase | `type CreateActionInput = { ... }` |
| Enums (as const objects) | PascalCase | `const SourceType = { ... } as const` |
| Constants | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `const MAX_ACTIONS_PER_SPEC = 50` |
| DB columns | camelCase TS / snake_case SQL | `sourceId` maps to `source_id` |

## Import Rules

```typescript
// 1. Use `import type` for type-only imports
import type { Spec } from '@stride/db';
import type { DrizzleDb } from '../lib/db';

// 2. Separate value imports from type imports
import { specRepo } from '../repos/spec.repo';
import { generateId } from '../lib/utils';

// 3. Use alias for default repo imports in services
import {
  specRepo as defaultSpecRepo,
  type SpecRepository,
} from '../repos/spec.repo';

// 4. Relative imports for same-package files
import { specsTable } from '../../packages/db/src/schema';

// 5. Package boundaries:
//    apps/web    → may import from packages/ui, packages/api-client, packages/queue
//    apps/api    → may import from packages/db only
//    apps/web    → must NOT import from apps/api directly (use packages/api-client)
//    packages/db → must NOT import from apps/api or apps/web
```

## Type Definitions

**Enums — `as const` objects, NOT TypeScript `enum`:**
```typescript
// CORRECT
export const SourceType = {
  JIRA: 'jira',
  LINEAR: 'linear',
  GITHUB: 'github',
} as const;
export type SourceType = (typeof SourceType)[keyof typeof SourceType];

// WRONG
export enum SourceType { JIRA = 'jira' }
```

**Entities — `type`, not `interface`:**
```typescript
// CORRECT
export type Spec = { id: string; title: string; sourceType: SourceType };

// WRONG
export interface Spec { ... }
```

**Inputs/DTOs — also `type`:**
```typescript
export type CreateActionInput = {
  title: string;
  specId?: string;
  estimate?: number;
};
```

**Always use `type`, never `interface`** — for entities, inputs, props, everything.

**Exports — barrel pattern:**
```typescript
// packages/db/src/index.ts
export type { Spec, Action, Session } from './schema';
export { insertSpecSchema, selectSpecSchema } from './schema';
export { SourceType } from './enums';
```

**One type/enum per file.**
